.SH MARKET DYNAMICS
The commodity market fluctuates based on supply and demand:
.IP \(bu 2
Prices update each round after both players complete turns
.IP \(bu 2
Buying increases demand, pushing prices up
.IP \(bu 2
Selling increases supply, pushing prices down
.IP \(bu 2
Random market forces also affect prices
.IP \(bu 2
Prices clamped to 50%-200% of base value
.PP
Use \fBmarket\fR to view current prices and trends, then \fBtrade buy/sell\fR to act.

.SH FACILITIES
Facilities at star systems provide strategic advantages to the controlling player.
Control is established by occupying a system with no enemy ships for 2 consecutive turns.
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Facility|Effect
SHIPYARD|Build new ships
REPAIR_DOCK|Repair damaged ships away from base
REFINERY|Fabrication bonuses
TRADE_HUB|+5 CR income per turn
FORTRESS|Combat defensive bonus
.TE
.PP
Use \fBrepair\fR at captured REPAIR_DOCKs or SHIPYARDs to repair ships in the field.

.SH AI AGENT PROGRAMMING
Kepler's Horizon supports single-player mode through an AI opponent whose behavior is defined in Kepler Script (KHS), a functional programming language tailored for tactical decision-making. The AI agent replaces one human player and executes commands through the same game systems, respecting all rules and inhibits.

.SS Overview
KHS scripts define AI strategy through a series of decision functions called during each phase of the AI's turn. The server loads
.I /opt/kepler/ai/strategy.khs
at startup and can reload it without restart via
.B kill -HUP
signal.

.SS Language Characteristics
KHS is a functional hybrid language combining immutability, pattern matching, and first-class functions with familiar C-like syntax:
.IP \(bu 2
Variables immutable by default (\fBconst\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Pattern matching via \fBmatch\fR expressions
.IP \(bu 2
Arrow functions for concise definitions
.IP \(bu 2
List comprehensions and pipe operators
.IP \(bu 2
C-like braces and semicolons (no whitespace sensitivity)
.IP \(bu 2
Strong typing with inference

.SS Reserved Words
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
Keyword|Purpose|Example
_
const|Immutable binding|const x = 5;
if|Conditional|if (x > 0) return true;
else|Alternative|else return false;
match|Pattern matching|match (tactic) { ... }
when|Match guard|when ratio < 0.3
return|Function result|return Attack;
for|List iteration|for ship in fleet
where|Filter condition|where ship.pd > 0
select|Map transform|select ship.location
.TE

